        "original_id": "475ef9cf-0334-53a8-bed9-8e242578e539",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Heavenly Creatures\n- People: Peter Jackson, Fran Walsh, Pauline Parker, Juliet Hulme, Anne Perry\n- Events: Parker–Hulme murder case\n- Places: Christchurch, New Zealand\n- Topics: psychological drama, historical detective fiction\n\nFacts:\n- The Parker–Hulme murder case occurred in 1954 in Christchurch, New Zealand.\n- Heavenly Creatures is a 1994 New Zealand psychological drama film directed by Peter Jackson.\n- Peter Jackson co-wrote the screenplay for Heavenly Creatures with Fran Walsh.\n- Heavenly Creatures is about the 1954 Parker–Hulme murder case.\n- Heavenly Creatures centers on the relationship between teenage girls Pauline Parker and Juliet Hulme.\n- In Heavenly Creatures, Pauline Parker and Juliet Hulme murder Parker's mother.\n- Anne Perry was born on 28 October 1938 as Juliet Marion Hulme.\n- Anne Perry is an English author of historical detective fiction.\n- Anne Perry is best known for the Thomas Pitt and William Monk series.",
